{
 "_comment": [
  "Hand-maintained starting goals per class, for players with no goals yet.",
  "Each class lists playstyles, the first one being the default. A playstyle's",
  "goals are in priority order, the same way the Goals panel orders them.",
  "Targets are mostly not stored: filling a preset starts each goal at the",
  "build's current value, so the planner looks for upgrades rather than chasing",
  "numbers nobody chose. A goal with a \"target\" (penetration at 50) keeps it",
  "while the build is short of it. confidence: \"from play\" / \"stated\" (class note names the stats)",
  "/ \"guess\" (read from skill scaling) / \"weak guess\" (skills are ambiguous).",
  "An empty list means the class has no combat to plan for.",
  "The playstyle offered first is the one the character's base stats lean",
  "towards (see sim/src/presets.ts). \"leans\" weighs the points put into each",
  "base stat; without it, the playstyle's own base-stat goals are used, each",
  "counting less the lower it is ranked. A negative lean counts against."
 ],
